{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite","id":1405233,"title":"Solar Presence rewrite","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-29T19:45:44-07:00","id":1405233,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Solar Presence rewrite","content":"Do you like Solars but hate how their social charms were less than stellar shortly after the corebook launch, let alone after Lunars? Would you love it if the charms had a little more punch while maintaining some resemblance of balance? Well I got news for you: I got bored. Which means nearly 40 or so charms appeared out of the ether.<br /> <br /> What can you expect with this rewrite?<ul><li>Rewriting of the Solar Presence tree from the ground up. Trust me: It needed it.</li> <li>Oodles of charms that do brand new things, while Exalted vets enjoy a trip down memory lane with a few official and fan favorites.</li> <li>Dedicated support for Manipulation focused Solars. No longer does Presence feel like Charisma: The Ability. You have plenty of support for your social actions and some very neat tricks of your own. Easily convince others to hand over the shoes, or tell them that the sky is purple they'll actually buy it.</li> <li>Minimal charm copying. I only needed to copy two Lunar charms. Technically 3, but the third existed in a charm I made 10 years ago so hell with it that doesn't count.</li> <li>Absolutely no play testing, as I just finished making these like an hour ago.</li> </ul><br /> Want to amaze those peasants? <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wkfPuphnrD6iDL6dSvjp8fdkyWCxFxYMPe5AxA_Lgcc/edit#heading=h.jitu187kg4fh\" target=\"_blank\">Then click here to find out in this one simple ability!</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T23:48:09-07:00","id":1405251,"title":"","content":"... You think Solar Presence is UNDER powered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T01:55:38-07:00","id":1405270,"title":"","content":"I mean he's got a point with it being very punishing to characters that want to empathize Manipulation or Appearance over Charisma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:15:41-07:00","id":1405285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405270#post1405270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean he's got a point with it being very punishing to characters that want to empathize Manipulation or Appearance over Charisma.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768056-is-appearance-kind-of-rubbish-or-am-i-missing-something?p=769441#post769441\">Holy 2015 Batman!</a><br /> <br /> There's <i>one</i> Charm in Solar Presence which excludes Manipulation (Mind-Wiping Gaze).<br /> <br /> And there's one Charm which excludes Appearance (Hypnotic Tongue Technique).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-30-2020, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:21:13-07:00","id":1405286,"title":"","content":"Whoah, you're right, my head-canon was... Head-canon, not canon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T06:52:23-07:00","id":1405323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405251#post1405251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... You think Solar Presence is UNDER powered?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could use a tune up. Which is what I did.<br /> <br /> As for Manipulation, it felt like it needed some more support. Impassioned Discourse Technique doesn't tell you what social attribute to use, but it's tone or intent screams Charisma. Maybe this may be anecdotal yes, but I've several other people who read into such things over the years. Plus there's plenty of other manipulation focused.<br /> <br /> Appearance is something else. I think that's fine(ish) already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T07:34:07-07:00","id":1405331,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm just a weirdo that takes unnecessary extra steps, but I've always made it a habit to ask my players what their tone or intent is in their social interactions before declaring what attribute needs to be used. It also gives them the opportunity to pause and think about their approach if I feel its one attribute over the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:49:01-07:00","id":1405350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405331#post1405331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm just a weirdo that takes unnecessary extra steps, but I've always made it a habit to ask my players what their tone or intent is in their social interactions before declaring what attribute needs to be used. It also gives them the opportunity to pause and think about their approach if I feel its one attribute over the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm open to other players using different attributes as well. Hell, I was allowing Appearance for social rolls back in 2.Xe. But it still doesn't stop with me feeling that Presence comes off as overly focused on Charisma in tone. Probably because Solars so far (and their stereotype) has been something akin to a DnD shiny golden paladin. Yes I know this is anecdotal, and we have an entire ability called Larceny that blows that out of the water, but it's still a stereotype I feel Solars have. Hell, my rewrite only has two charms that explicitly calls for Manipulation, and those are because I don't think Appearance fits them and what I feel furthest from Charisma you can possibly get. I mean I think the new branch I made in there is very much geared towards Manipulation users. I think using Charisma would be very difficult mental gymnastics, but if you come up with a reason how it applies then more power to you.<br /> <br /> However I think going any further into the topic of &quot;The three social attributes: When to use them&quot; is an entirely different conversation. One that I don't mind, but one that I don't think is appropriate for this thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:05:58-07:00","id":1405375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405323#post1405323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it could use a tune up. Which is what I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am never going to say that a Corebook Charmset doesn't need a tune-up. I won't be using your work, but I applaud your attempt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T04:31:10-07:00","id":1405543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405375#post1405375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't be using your work, but I applaud your attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be decent for somebody in this thread to actually go through the Charms in question, whether individually as a whole, and provide some critique of them. Even if one holds a premise that they don't express the Presence Ability, that might be best served through a breakdown of what the Charms do.<br /> <br /> A person sharing their work and getting several responses that collectively just disagree with the impulse behind having undertaken it in the first place strikes me as distinctly unfair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T06:35:48-07:00","id":1405560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405543#post1405543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be decent for somebody in this thread to actually go through the Charms in question, whether individually as a whole, and provide some critique of them. Even if one holds a premise that they don't express the Presence Ability, that might be best served through a breakdown of what the Charms do.<br /> <br /> A person sharing their work and getting several responses that collectively just disagree with the impulse behind having undertaken it in the first place strikes me as distinctly unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no interest in going through someone's fan work and listing all the things I hate about it. <br /> <br /> (If someone wants to pay me to copy-edit this, my rates are reasonable.)<br /> <br /> If you think this would be productive use of time, perhaps you'd like to do it yourself?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1183_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1183\" data-vbnamecard=\"1183\">Sandact6</a> To be absolutely clear: If you don't like something then you should change it. You've put together quite a lot of work here, and I'm grateful that you've shared it with the community. I hope people find it valuable.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I will not equivocate on my opinion<br /> I have always worn it on my sleeve<br /> Even if I said what you think I said<br /> You would need to cite a more specific grievance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T07:07:26-07:00","id":1405565,"title":"","content":"Going through someone's work and pointing out flaws, what you dislike, and what you hate isn't really called shitting on it, it's called critique (Yes there's a difference between dislike and hate). I had my work been called terrible, worthless, a waste of time, and outright stolen before. As long was one gives reasons for their opinions I'm likely to accept them, otherwise I toss them into the wastebasket of my mind as it contains nothing that could better improve my work. The only thing your review would be are words, and I'd seriously doubt they'd hurt me of all people.<br /> <br /> I don't expect anyone to go through each charm individually, there's too many there. I would however like to hear why you wouldn't be using it (Be it the remade or the new charms), even if it were only one or two sentences. Do you find them shit in some capacity? Are they broken? Are they unoriginal? Are you using some sort of Exalted mechanical alternative (Quixlated, ExWod, the several charm rewrites I've seen on the form) that make it redundant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:11:37-07:00","id":1405581,"title":"","content":"Personally I wouldn't use it because to me Presence <i>is</i> &quot;Charisma: The Ability&quot;. I prefer the Charms with the explicit flavors of conning people, lying to them and manipulating them to stay in the realms of Larceny and Socialize.<br /> <br /> Here's a critique of the first few Charm, might do more later if I have time:<br /> <br /> <b>Exemplar of Virtue Demonstration</b> - should probably limit either the intensity of the Principle that can trigger this, or the intensity that can be instilled in others. For instance, should the Charm allow someone to take their Minor Principle and strengthen it to the Defining level in someone else who already has it at Major?<br /> <br /> <b>Begruging Respect Acceptance</b> and <b>Shameful Action Retort</b> both feel properly Solar, good stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Impassioned Discourse Technique &amp; Shrouded Night's Tongue</b> - There seems to be nothing preventing me from using Shrouded Night's Tongue without doing anything that would provoke penalties, so the Charm is basically E1, 3m for 3-5 non-Charm dice. Besides being way OP as dice adders go, it also makes Impassioned Discourse Technique worthless since they're both mutually exclusive and the latter does the exact same thing, except with 3-5 Charm dice instead of non-Charm dice.<br /> <br /> <b>Overlooking Innocent Transgressions</b> - preventing someone from being offended by things that go against their defining without a chance to resist sounds roleplay-breaking, to be honest. Maybe increase the cost to more than 1wp or something if the target doesn't hate the Solar?<br /> <br /> <b>Faithful Words Prana</b> - the wording was not clear to me, had to read multiple times to understand what it does. The Charm sounds more Lunar than Solar but otherwise fine.<br /> <br /> <b>Duplicitous Wordsmith Obfuscation</b> - I don't like that it can suppress a Defining as easily as a Minor, otherwise fine.<br /> <br /> <b>Tripping the Bumbling Fool</b> - Cool flavor, I'm just not sure about the &quot;cannot face the Solar&quot; effect, feels like on some characters that will be, well, out of character.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T09:53:49-07:00","id":1405598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405581#post1405581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I wouldn't use it because to me Presence <i>is</i> &quot;Charisma: The Ability&quot;. I prefer the Charms with the explicit flavors of conning people, lying to them and manipulating them to stay in the realms of Larceny and Socialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. It's something I don't necessarily agree with but fair nonetheless. In fact I planned on sharing many of the Manipulation focused charms directly into Socialize as I feel that Solar Socialize desperately needs some attention. I won't guess it's power, but it's like looking at a grey square whereas the DB Socialize set is akin to looking at a rainbow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405581#post1405581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Exemplar of Virtue Demonstration</b> - should probably limit either the intensity of the Principle that can trigger this, or the intensity that can be instilled in others. For instance, should the Charm allow someone to take their Minor Principle and strengthen it to the Defining level in someone else who already has it at Major?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about putting it at Major or defining but decided against it. I felt it placed too little emphasis on Minor principles and would make them feel worthless in comparison.<br /> <br /> And RAW yes that's exactly how it's written. I thought it'd be fitting that if you're a literal god king (and going down this 'arc' you pretty much are playing up that stereotype) then people will fanatically defend both you and even the things you feel not as strongly about because you're that damn good at speaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405581#post1405581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Impassioned Discourse Technique &amp; Shrouded Night's Tongue</b> - There seems to be nothing preventing me from using Shrouded Night's Tongue without doing anything that would provoke penalties, so the Charm is basically E1, 3m for 3-5 non-Charm dice. Besides being way OP as dice adders go, it also makes Impassioned Discourse Technique worthless since they're both mutually exclusive and the latter does the exact same thing, except with 3-5 Charm dice instead of non-Charm dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at Heart-Snaring Deception in Lunars. The main thing this charm does is combine the +1 from Glib Tongue Technique and add it here (As Listener-Swaying is a catch all for any social action). Secondly this charm is powered by using the <i>target's</i> intimacies, not yours. This is a key theme for manipulators in general, both in games and IRL.<br /> <br /> The thing is Charisma isn't that good at making implausible claims like manipulation is I feel. I mean you certainly can get rolls like that, but I'm willing to bet most ST's will probably make such a claim a manipulation roll. Likewise Impassioned Discourse is good for speaking from the heart. I don't tell you what attribute it can be used for, but I'm willing to bet Charisma first by a wide margin, then Appearance, then Manipulation trailing behind. Last this charm is powered by <i>your</i> intimacies. The opponent's don't factor into this charm.<br /> <br /> Still you are correct in that they feel functionally identical. I might do a price break thing, saying you can buy one charm for a cheaper price if you have the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405581#post1405581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Overlooking Innocent Transgressions</b> - preventing someone from being offended by things that go against their defining without a chance to resist sounds roleplay-breaking, to be honest. Maybe increase the cost to more than 1wp or something if the target doesn't hate the Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>The precedent for this charm already exists in Socialize (Indecent Proposal Method). I could slap the ability to make people offended by spending a WP, would that work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405581#post1405581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Faithful Words Prana</b> - the wording was not clear to me, had to read multiple times to understand what it does. The Charm sounds more Lunar than Solar but otherwise fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have suggestions to improve the clarity? The second sentence of the charm describes exactly what it does, I thought that would've been sufficient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405581#post1405581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tripping the Bumbling Fool</b> - Cool flavor, I'm just not sure about the &quot;cannot face the Solar&quot; effect, feels like on some characters that will be, well, out of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if the opponent has many intimacies related to confrontation or really hates the Solar, it wouldn't be too long for them to get rid of this charm. The idea is that you were made such a fool out of that even the most rash of people will go &quot;Oh shit, I need to take a step back for a moment and figure out what to do next as I have <i>no</i> idea what to do next&quot;.<br /> <br /> Again the intent is that Righteous Lion Defence can trump this intimacy. If the guarded intimacy would somehow allow you to continue, then you can still do so. You'd be at a disadvantage as the audience thinks you're an ignorant buffoon, but this was also a soft measure to a player/NPC to ask &quot;Hey, do you really want to continue this?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T09:54:00-07:00","id":1405599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405565#post1405565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would however like to hear why you wouldn't be using it (Be it the remade or the new charms), even if it were only one or two sentences. Do you find them shit in some capacity? Are they broken? Are they unoriginal? Are you using some sort of Exalted mechanical alternative (Quixlated, ExWod, the several charm rewrites I've seen on the form) that make it redundant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the social system.<br /> <br /> I like that the best way to get people to do stuff for you is using what they already care about. A cursory reading suggests your Charms exacerbate my two biggest gripes with the system -- &quot;you suddenly care about X for no reason&quot; and &quot;this action TOTALLY supports your intimacy, wink!&quot;<br /> <br /> Your Charms feel very much like UMI. It's less &quot;my Solar is very convincing&quot; and more Solar Mind Control.<br /> <br /> I also don't share the fundamental reasoning behind your Charms. &quot;This Charm adds three dice to your social rolls&quot; helps manipulative characters. &quot;This Charm lets you seduce people who aren't attracted to you&quot; also helps Manipulative characters.<br /> <br /> It's not that your Charms are bad, it's that for me to use them they'd have to be better than the official Charms at expressing Solar themes. And not just better, but so much better that it's worthwhile printing them out and teaching them to my players.<br /> <br /> If I'm going to rewrite entire Charm trees, I may as well rewrite the game.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't want to balance check your Charms for you. Vetting 40 custom charms is work. Playtesting an entire Charmset is work.<br /> <br /> I'd be eager to see how these hold up in play.<br /> <br /> I agree with you the Charmset could use a tune up. I'm more interested in what Essence does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T10:21:39-07:00","id":1405610,"title":"","content":"OK, fair enough. I may not agree with your opinions but I respect them nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Also I'm not holding a gun to a person's head and demanding for a review of every individual part. Even a general overview going &quot;I think this are too over/underpowered&quot; or what you just posted there is perfectly fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T11:16:19-07:00","id":1405624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405598#post1405598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at Heart-Snaring Deception in Lunars. The main thing this charm does is combine the +1 from Glib Tongue Technique and add it here (As Listener-Swaying is a catch all for any social action). Secondly this charm is powered by using the <i>target's</i> intimacies, not yours. This is a key theme for manipulators in general, both in games and IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar Charm can explicitly only be rolled with Manipulation, this one doesn't state any restrictions like that. You're much more likely to have penalties for implausible claims, outlandish requests or rude tone on a Manipulation roll than on a Charisma roll, so simply by not having that same restriction you end up with a Charm that is stronger because it's much more broadly applicable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405598#post1405598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The precedent for this charm already exists in Socialize (Indecent Proposal Method). I could slap the ability to make people offended by spending a WP, would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh nevermind then, I guess I just don't like the Core Charm it's based on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405598#post1405598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have suggestions to improve the clarity? The second sentence of the charm describes exactly what it does, I thought that would've been sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>You can use a Positive Tie the target holds towards you as if it were an applicable Intimacy for the purpose of supporting your Persuade action. The Intimacy must still be of the appropriate intensity for the seriousness of the task.</i><br /> <br /> At least if I understood what the Charm does correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T12:44:44-07:00","id":1405654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405624#post1405624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar Charm can explicitly only be rolled with Manipulation, this one doesn't state any restrictions like that. You're much more likely to have penalties for implausible claims, outlandish requests or rude tone on a Manipulation roll than on a Charisma roll, so simply by not having that same restriction you end up with a Charm that is stronger because it's much more broadly applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was tempted to enforce a Manipulation roll for this, but fell short of actually putting that in as I thought there was almost no way it could be used for Charisma. However in hindsight, seeing as how a Charisma focused character could grab this for free dice, I'll put that back in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405624#post1405624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>You can use a Positive Tie the target holds towards you as if it were an applicable Intimacy for the purpose of supporting your Persuade action. The Intimacy must still be of the appropriate intensity for the seriousness of the task.</i><br /> <br /> At least if I understood what the Charm does correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intention was to also let it be used in bargain actions. Think of it kinda like needing a loan. You don't have any collateral to offer up and for all intents and purposes seems like a really bad deal for the lender. But they think &quot;You know what, something tells me I can trust this guy&quot; and they give you the money anyways. Another example is if you're debating academics with someone else, you can say &quot;I'm pretty sure the history X event went like this&quot; and then completely lie about it. Even if the opponent used a declare fact roll to make it true, the person you're trying to convince will trust you who has far more credentials in history knowledge than you.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, would this be clearer?<br /> <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can use a Positive Tie the target holds towards you as if it were an applicable Intimacy, tangible resource, or experience required for the purpose of supporting your Persuade or bargain action.</span></span></b></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T14:45:23-07:00","id":1405669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1405233-solar-presence-rewrite?p=1405654#post1405654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b><span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can use a Positive Tie the target holds towards you as if it were an applicable Intimacy, tangible resource, or experience required for the purpose of supporting your Persuade or bargain action.</span></span></b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>When you say tangible resource, do you mean like Resource the merit or something else? Like how is it measured?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T15:34:59-07:00","id":1405678,"title":"","content":"Pretty much exclusively resources yes, but also something valuable. Bargain actions don't need to be strictly resources, but you can also swap favors with it as well.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> Barbarian: &quot;I'll help you, but I want the sword of Aman-Ra first.&quot;<br /> Solar: &quot;Funny, I was <i>just</i> going in the direction where the Aman-Ra is. Help me and I'll bring it to you on the way back.&quot; *Activates Faithful Words Prana*<br /> Barbarian: &quot;Very well, I will agree to help.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cus